; The weapon chest, a short walk from the spawn. It holds a PREFERENCE, not an object:
; `contains` is an ordered list and what comes out is the first entry the opener has never
; found, so the same chest would hand over the bow if the axe were already yours. The
; sword is not listed because the player starts holding it — components/loadout.gd records
; the starting item as found for exactly this reason.
;
; One chest gives one item, because Interactable.one_shot is what makes a chest a chest.
; The other three arrive as more chests, or immediately via the F4 debug cycle.
[node name="Chest_weapons" type="Area3D" parent="World/Gameplay"]
transform = Transform3D(0.9, 0, -0.4358899, 0, 1, 0, 0.4358899, 0, 0.9, 9, 0, 14)
script = ExtResource("7_hx10c")
contains = Array[ItemData]([ExtResource("18_axe"), ExtResource("19_bow"), ExtResource("20_shield")])
chest_id = "village_weapons"

