; THE SPARRING GROUND. Two straw dummies on the flat west of the campfire — the first
; lockable, hittable things in this world, and the reason lock-on is playable rather
; than merely implemented.
;
; EVERY NUMBER HERE IS MEASURED, and the placement went through three wrong answers
; before this one. A raycast sweep of the clearing puts flat ground at y=0 across
; x -6..12 / z 0..6 and x -6..4 / z 6..18, with the village plateau at 3.4 m taking
; x 9..13 / z 7..11, the lookout at 3.9 m taking x <= -8, and the river trench at
; -0.7 m taking z -2..-6. Both dummies also drop themselves onto whatever is under
; them on load, so a Y here is a starting point rather than a claim.
;
; What ruled out the first two spots was not the ground but the CAMERA. A pair at
; (9.5, 3) and (12, 4) looked ideal until the sight-line from the camera eye to the
; nearer one was traced and came back blocked by House3's collision body; a pair at
; (5, 1) and (8, 2.5) locked and framed correctly but a village house then filled the
; right third of the photographed frame.
;
; The third consideration is why they are up HERE, at z 13-15.5, rather than in the
; middle of the field. All twenty existing legibility shots stand at z <= 12.5 and
; look down -Z, so anything at z >= 13 is behind every one of their cameras — checked
; per shot, including the 5 m sight-line from the spawn shot's own eye at (2.5, 17.67),
; where both dummies fall 54 and 64 degrees off axis. Adding an actor to a hand-edited
; level should not silently change twenty frames that have already been judged.
;
; Their SEPARATION is deliberate and it is on display. From the shot position south of
; them, the NEARER dummy sits further from the centre of frame than the further one, so
; pressing target locks the one 7.1 m away rather than the one 4.8 m away — the visible
; proof that selection is screen-space distance from the centre of frame and never 3D
; range. tools/probe.gd asserts the same thing against targets it builds itself.
[node name="TargetDummy_north" parent="World/Gameplay" instance=ExtResource("21_dummy")]
transform = Transform3D(0.9781476, 0, 0.20791169, 0, 1, 0, -0.20791169, 0, 0.9781476, -2, 0, 15.5)

[node name="TargetDummy_west" parent="World/Gameplay" instance=ExtResource("21_dummy")]
transform = Transform3D(0.8660254, 0, -0.5, 0, 1, 0, 0.5, 0, 0.8660254, -4, 0, 13)

